unit:ARCSEC
  a qudt:DerivedUnit, qudt:Unit ;
  dcterms:description """An arcsecond, also called a $\\textit{second of arc}$, is a unit of angle equal to $1/60$ arcminutes, or
    1/1296000 of a turn. The recommended symbol for the arcsecond in the is the $\\textit{double prime}$ ($''$). In combination
    with prefixes, the symbol $as$ has also become common, like in astronomy, where very small angles are stated in
