unit:AT
  a qudt:DerivedUnit, qudt:Unit ;
  dcterms:description """The $\\textit{ampere-turn}$ was the MKS unit of magnetomotive force (MMF), represented by a direct
    current of one ampere flowing in a single-turn loop in a vacuum. "Turns" refers to the winding number of an electrical
    conductor comprising an inductor. The ampere-turn was replaced by the SI unit, $ampere$.
  """^^qudt:LatexString ;
