unit:BYTE
  a qudt:CountingUnit, qudt:DerivedUnit, qudt:Unit ;
  dcterms:description """A <em>byte</em> is a unit of digital information that most commonly consists of eight bits. As a counting
    unit it measures data volume or storage capacity (one byte = 8 bits).
  <p>For the distinction between this counting sense and the information-entropy sense (the shannon), see
  <a href="../vocab/unit#BIT">unit:BIT</a>.</p>
  """^^rdf:HTML ;
