unit:L
  a qudt:Unit ;
  dcterms:description """The $litre$ (American spelling: $\\textit{liter}$; SI symbol $l$ or $L$) is a non-SI metric system unit
    of volume equal to $1 \\textit{cubic decimetre}$ ($dm^3$), 1,000 cubic centimetres ($cm^3$) or $1/1000 \\textit{cubic metre}$.
    If the lower case "L" is used as the symbol, it is sometimes rendered as a cursive "l" to help distinguish it from the capital
    "I", although this usage has no official approval by any international bureau.
  """^^qudt:LatexString ;
