    contained in a volume of one cubic foot at reference temperature and pressure conditions. As such, it is a measure of the
    actual amount of gas, not the volume of the gas. The reference conditions for standard cubic foot per minute are 60 degrees
    Fahrenheit and 14.7 pounds per square inch (psi) of pressure.
  """^^qudt:LatexString ;
  qudt:conversionMultiplier 0.0003328055555555555555555555555555556 ;
  qudt:conversionMultiplierSN 3.328055555555555555555555555555556E-4 ;
